## Post-generation: run the code generator

The generated `.dart` files are **hand-authored annotated source**. Dart's macro
support was cancelled, so the companion `*.freezed.dart` and `*.g.dart` files are
produced by `build_runner`. After generating (or regenerating) the models, run:

```bash
dart pub get
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```

This produces the freezed unions and the `fromJson` / `toJson` implementations
the models reference via their `part` directives.

## Layout

- `{{ models_dir }}/` — freezed model classes, the `enums.dart` file, and the
  `models_index.dart` barrel.
- `lib/{{ package_name }}/core/converters.dart` — JsonConverters bridging
  Dart types (`Decimal`, `Uint8List`, `DateTime`) to the backend's wire format.

## Wire compatibility

Models deserialize the same JSON the FastAPI backend (generated from the same
spec) emits: money as decimal **strings**, timestamps as ISO8601 + `Z`, binary
as base64, and enum members as `UPPER_CASE`.
